// Crazy Eights — 3 players, shed all your cards.
//
// Rules:
//   - Each player is dealt 5 cards; one card starts the Discard pile.
//   - On your turn, play **exactly one card that matches** the top of the
//     Discard pile — same rank or same suit — or any 8 (wild). The engine
//     only offers matching cards (the play prompt lists them), so plays are
//     always legal.
//   - If you cannot play (no match, no 8), you **must** draw one card.
//   - After playing (or being forced to draw), you may draw one card and
//     give it to *any* player — a house rule.
//   - The game ends when the deck runs out, a player empties their hand,
//     or after 30 turns; the player with the fewest cards wins.
//
// Remaining house rules / deviations (documented, not hidden):
//   - Declining both the play and the voluntary draw passes the turn
//     entirely (the DSL's `optional` has no else-branch to force a draw on
//     decline — D-3).
//   - The "hand empty" end condition is only checked when the current
//     player's turn starts, so a win is detected with up to one round of
//     delay (the 30-turn cap guarantees termination).
//
// Engine notes:
//   - Playing uses `move 1 from Hand where (...) of current`, which prompts
//     the player to pick exactly ONE matching card (2026-08-10 verb
//     semantics: `move N` = pick N cards; `deal N` = automatic top N).
//   - The match filter reads the top of the Discard pile live:
//     `Rank is Rank of top(Discard) or (Suit is Suit of top(Discard) or
//     Rank is "Eight")`.
//   - Drawing uses `Hand of any`, which prompts for a player
//     (InputType::ChoosePlayer).

player P1, P2, P3
turnorder (P:P1, P:P2, P:P3)
location Hand on all
location Deck on table
location Discard on table

card on Deck:
  Rank(Ace, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven, Eight, Nine, Ten, Jack, Queen, King)
    for Suit(Diamonds, Clubs, Hearts, Spades)

shuffle Deck

stage Deal for current 1 times {
  deal 5 from Deck private to Hand of all
  deal 1 from Deck private to Discard
}

stage Play for current until (Deck empty or Hand of current empty) or 30 times {
  if (not Hand where (Rank is Rank of top(Discard) or (Suit is Suit of top(Discard) or Rank is "Eight")) of current empty) {
    optional {
      move 1 from Hand where (Rank is Rank of top(Discard) or (Suit is Suit of top(Discard) or Rank is "Eight")) of current private to Discard
    }
  }
  if (Hand where (Rank is Rank of top(Discard) or (Suit is Suit of top(Discard) or Rank is "Eight")) of current empty) {
    if (not Deck empty) {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of current
    }
  }
  if (not Deck empty) {
    optional {
      deal 1 from Deck private to Hand of any
    }
  }
  cycle to next
}

stage Score for current 3 times {
  score size(cards Hand of current) to current
  cycle to next
}

stage End for current 1 times {
  winner is lowest score
}
